steps.text:
`OutlinedInput` passes an `inputRef` prop to its `inputComponent`. `TextareaAutosize` doesn’t consume that prop, so it gets forwarded to the native `<textarea>`, causing the warning.

Use a small adapter that maps `inputRef` to `ref` and removes it from the DOM props:

```jsx
const OutlinedTextarea = React.forwardRef(function OutlinedTextarea(props, ref) {
  const { inputRef, ...other } = props;

  return <TextareaAutosize
    {...other}
    ref={inputRef || ref}
  />;
});

<OutlinedInput inputComponent={OutlinedTextarea} />
```

This is expected when supplying a custom `inputComponent`: it must handle Material-UI’s `inputRef` contract rather than forwarding that prop unchanged.
